# Spendr

Personal-finance mobile app. Design: https://www.figma.com/design/oKN131gbYKd6PRyz4Gsydb/Design-Spendr-Mobile-App-UI

## Core rules

1. **Clean React + TypeScript** — functional components, explicit types, one responsibility per file; no `any` unless unavoidable.
2. **Premium dark fintech UI** — preserve the existing look: dark gradients, glass cards, brand accents, subtle motion. Do not flatten or lighten the theme.
3. **Reusable components** — extract shared UI into `src/app/components/`; use `src/app/components/ui/` (shadcn) before creating duplicates.
4. **Zustand for state** — client/UI state lives in `src/store/`; do not add Redux, Context-heavy trees, or duplicate auth listeners.
5. **Firebase backend** — Auth + Firestore via `src/lib/firebase.ts` and hooks in `src/hooks/`; server reads/writes use TanStack Query where already established.
6. **Never expose API keys** — use `VITE_*` env vars in `.env.local` only; never commit secrets, log keys, or hardcode credentials in source.
7. **Avoid unnecessary dependencies** — prefer existing stack (Vite, React Router, Tailwind, motion, lucide); justify any new package.
8. **Mobile-first responsive** — max-width **430px** column in `RootLayout`; test layouts at phone widths first.
9. **Scalable folder structure** — keep the layout below; add files in the correct layer, not at repo root.
10. **Minimal diffs** — change only files required for the task; do not refactor or reformat unrelated code.
11. **Beginner-friendly architecture** — predictable paths, named exports, thin screens, logic in hooks/stores; avoid deep abstractions or clever indirection.
12. **Production-grade practices** — typed env handling, query invalidation after mutations, guarded routes, error feedback on auth/API failures.

## Stack

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Build | Vite 6, React 18, TypeScript |
| Routing | React Router 7 — `src/app/routes.tsx` |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS 4 — `src/styles/` |
| Backend | Firebase Auth + Firestore |
| Server state | TanStack Query — `src/hooks/` |
| Client state | Zustand — `src/store/` |
| Motion | `motion/react` |
| Icons | `lucide-react` |

## Folder structure

``
src/
  app/
    screens/          # Full-page views
    components/       # Shared app components (BottomNav, etc.)
    components/ui/    # shadcn primitives — avoid casual edits
    routes.tsx
    App.tsx
  hooks/              # Firestore + React Query hooks
  store/              # Zustand stores
  lib/                # firebase.ts, utils
  styles/
```

New protected screens: add to `routes.tsx` under `<ProtectedRoute />` and update `BottomNav` when tab-visible.

## UI standards

- Root: `className="dark"`; backgrounds `black` / `#0a0a14`; cards `bg-white/5 backdrop-blur border-white/10`
- Accents: `#00d9ff`, `#00ff88`, `#9d4edd`, `#ff6b35`, `#ffd60a`, `#ff3366`
- Bottom nav: max **5** tabs; keep route paths in sync
- Match existing motion patterns (`initial` / `animate`, soft gradient orbs)

## Data & security

- Auth: `useAuthStore` — single `onAuthStateChanged` subscription
- Users: Firestore `users/{uid}` via `useUserData`; invalidate queries after writes
- Onboarding: `useOnboardingStore` + `useOnboarding` hook
- Copy `.env.example` → `.env.local`; never commit `.env.local`

## Commands

```bash
npm install && npm run dev
npm run build
```
